            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "Testing a fractional candidate,\n$$\\begin{aligned}P\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=\\frac12-\\frac72+\\frac{15}{2}-\\frac{13}{2}+2\\\\&=0\\\\P'(x)&=32x^3-84x^2+60x-13\\\\P'\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=4-21+30-13=0\\\\P''(x)&=96x^2-168x+60\\\\P''\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=24-84+60=0\\\\P'''(x)&=192x-168\\\\P'''\\left(\\frac12\\right)&=-72\\ne0.\\end{aligned}$$Thus $x=\\dfrac12$ is the triple zero.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the remaining simple zero, and hence factor $P(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Remaining simple zero: $x=2$.\n\n$P(x)=(2x-1)^3(x-2)$. ",
          "worked": "Let the remaining zero be $r$. Using the sum of roots,\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac12+\\frac12+\\frac12+r&=\\frac{28}{8}\\\\r&=2\\\\P(x)&=8\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)^3(x-2)\\\\&=(2x-1)^3(x-2).\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
